[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m \[ x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m This can be factored as:
[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m \[ (x-2)(x-3) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m So, the roots are \( x = 2 \) and \( x = 3 \). The quadratic expression \( x^2 - 5x + 6 \) is a parabola that opens upwards. It is positive outside the interval \([2, 3]\) and negative inside this interval. Therefore, the inequality \( x^2 - 5x + 6 > 0 \) holds for:
[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m \[ x \in (-\infty, 2) \cup (3, \infty) \]
[36m(main_task pid=3408)[0m 
